WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:02.856
- Hello all of the internet, I'm Gav.

00:00:02.856 --> 00:00:03.689
- I'm Dan.

00:00:03.689 --> 00:00:04.724
- We're The Slow Mo Guys,

00:00:04.724 --> 00:00:07.435
and yes, it is that time of year again.

00:00:07.435 --> 00:00:10.266
We've got another six foot,
giant red balloon here.

00:00:10.266 --> 00:00:11.099
- Classic.

00:00:11.099 --> 00:00:12.133
Done a few of those now, haven't we?

00:00:12.133 --> 00:00:12.966
- Yeah, we have.

00:00:12.966 --> 00:00:14.139
- Done you jumping on a
big ballon full of water.

00:00:14.139 --> 00:00:14.972
- On it.

00:00:14.972 --> 00:00:16.025
- Me in a big balloon full of water.

00:00:16.025 --> 00:00:16.858
- In it.

00:00:16.858 --> 00:00:18.395
- Me in a big balloon full of air.

00:00:18.395 --> 00:00:19.472
- In it.

00:00:19.472 --> 00:00:20.375
- So, what's next?

00:00:20.375 --> 00:00:21.250
- Under it.

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:22.083
- Under it?

00:00:22.083 --> 00:00:22.916
- I think under it.

00:00:22.916 --> 00:00:24.511
So we've got this trampoline,

00:00:24.511 --> 00:00:25.476
and we'll put this on you,

00:00:25.476 --> 00:00:26.425
and start to fill it with water

00:00:26.425 --> 00:00:28.241
until it either pops,

00:00:28.241 --> 00:00:30.594
or you get crushed to death.

00:00:30.594 --> 00:00:32.349
- Brilliant. I know which one's best.

00:00:32.349 --> 00:00:34.621
I like that your idea of
me being crushed to death

00:00:34.621 --> 00:00:36.377
is being made more comfortable

00:00:36.377 --> 00:00:37.210
by being on a trampoline.

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:38.043
- Yeah, bit softer.

00:00:38.043 --> 00:00:38.876
- Ah you'll be fine.

00:00:38.876 --> 00:00:39.709
- Softer than the ground,

00:00:39.709 --> 00:00:42.473
and also the water won't
pool around you when it pops,

00:00:42.473 --> 00:00:43.319
it'll just go straight through.

00:00:43.319 --> 00:00:44.152
- Considerate.

00:00:44.152 --> 00:00:45.154
It's very considerate.
- Very considerate.

00:00:45.154 --> 00:00:47.015
- This is the first in a series of videos

00:00:47.015 --> 00:00:50.515
that I'm going to call Giant Balloon June.

00:00:51.724 --> 00:00:53.333
Which, honestly I'm
quite proud of that name.

00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:54.166
- Well done, well done.

00:00:54.166 --> 00:00:54.999
Yep, yep.
- So we'll be doing

00:00:54.999 --> 00:00:56.368
just giant balloon videos in June.

00:00:56.368 --> 00:00:57.793
We'll try and get a few of them out,

00:00:57.793 --> 00:01:00.199
and let's start with this one.

00:01:00.199 --> 00:01:01.032
- All right.

00:01:01.032 --> 00:01:02.911
- Off we go.

00:01:02.911 --> 00:01:04.198
- [Gavin] Cue the sun!

00:01:04.198 --> 00:01:05.452
- Oh I'm excited to be doing another

00:01:05.452 --> 00:01:06.938
water ballon video actually.

00:01:06.938 --> 00:01:07.771
- [Gavin] Yeah.

00:01:07.771 --> 00:01:09.257
- It's just like this is
bringing back old memories.

00:01:09.257 --> 00:01:10.660
- [Gavin] We're experts
at this, aren't we?

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:11.565
- Pretty good.

00:01:11.565 --> 00:01:12.398
- [Gavin] All right,

00:01:12.398 --> 00:01:13.618
we're just moistening down the trampoline

00:01:13.618 --> 00:01:16.690
just to get the black material cooler,

00:01:16.690 --> 00:01:18.280
because it's been
absorbing heat all morning.

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:21.671
Okay so position the balloon on yourself.

00:01:21.671 --> 00:01:23.116
- Just on my crotchal region.

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:25.362
- [Gavin] Just cause it's so ridiculous.

00:01:25.362 --> 00:01:26.214
All right, here we go.

00:01:26.214 --> 00:01:27.638
- [Daniel] Thing is,

00:01:27.638 --> 00:01:29.034
I'm not even going to be
getting the benefit of the water

00:01:29.034 --> 00:01:30.514
because I'm not going to be in the water.

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:32.624
Could be wrong here.

00:01:32.624 --> 00:01:33.991
That's already heavy.

00:01:33.991 --> 00:01:35.251
- [Gavin] Is it?

00:01:35.251 --> 00:01:36.084
- Yeah.

00:01:40.616 --> 00:01:42.982
Getting a really good shot
of my double chin here.

00:01:42.982 --> 00:01:44.286
- [Gavin] Well the beard covers it,

00:01:44.286 --> 00:01:45.194
doesn't it?

00:01:45.194 --> 00:01:46.806
- Not the comfiest thing in the world.

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:47.639
- [Gavin] No?

00:01:47.639 --> 00:01:48.472
- No.

00:01:48.472 --> 00:01:50.211
Don't think it would be
a good fashion accessory.

00:01:50.211 --> 00:01:52.805
Oh, it's all going to glob
over the side of me soon.

00:01:52.805 --> 00:01:54.283
I think I'm stuck now.

00:01:55.297 --> 00:01:56.297
- That's it.

00:01:57.313 --> 00:01:59.235
- [Gavin] It looks like
you've got a big bean.

00:02:00.908 --> 00:02:01.852
Does it look comfy?

00:02:01.852 --> 00:02:02.950
- [Gavin] It looks quite nice.

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:03.783
Is it cool?

00:02:03.783 --> 00:02:04.616
- Yeah.

00:02:04.616 --> 00:02:06.017
It's cool without being wet.

00:02:06.017 --> 00:02:07.150
- [Gavin] I reckon I'm
hotter than you are.

00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:08.733
- You probably are.

00:02:12.357 --> 00:02:14.274
Sounds like laser fire.

00:02:17.368 --> 00:02:19.099
- [Gavin] Had to get a
higher angle on the Phantom

00:02:19.099 --> 00:02:20.782
because he's sinking so much.

00:02:22.288 --> 00:02:23.728
Do you think people weigh this much?

00:02:23.728 --> 00:02:24.948
How much does this weigh?

00:02:24.948 --> 00:02:26.591
- [Gavin] Yeah, people
weigh way more than that.

00:02:26.591 --> 00:02:28.330
- How much is the heaviest person?

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:29.703
- [Gavin] Over a thousand pounds.

00:02:29.703 --> 00:02:30.536
- No.

00:02:30.536 --> 00:02:31.412
- [Gavin] Yeah.

00:02:31.412 --> 00:02:32.245
- A thousand pounds?

00:02:32.245 --> 00:02:33.453
- [Gavin] Think so.

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:34.573
- What's that? 500 kilos?

00:02:34.573 --> 00:02:36.945
I'm going to try and move my legs.

00:02:36.945 --> 00:02:37.778
- Ready?

00:02:37.778 --> 00:02:38.611
- [Gavin] Yeah.

00:02:38.611 --> 00:02:39.444
- Right.

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:45.232
- I almost pooped myself then.

00:02:46.356 --> 00:02:48.689
- Hang on, let me try again.

00:02:52.482 --> 00:02:53.315
Oh, I just farted.

00:02:53.315 --> 00:02:54.291
Oh, god.

00:02:54.291 --> 00:02:55.793
Oh, I just guffed, did you hear that?

00:02:55.793 --> 00:02:57.317
- [Gavin] Yeah.

00:02:58.575 --> 00:03:01.975
- [Gavin] That was awful.

00:03:01.975 --> 00:03:04.013
You over-exerted yourself.

00:03:04.013 --> 00:03:05.536
- I almost had a hernia.

00:03:06.954 --> 00:03:07.821
- Flipping heck.

00:03:07.821 --> 00:03:09.166
- [Gavin] What is this video?

00:03:09.166 --> 00:03:09.999
I don't know.

00:03:12.207 --> 00:03:15.035
Man prolapses trying to get
out from under a big balloon.

00:03:15.035 --> 00:03:15.868
- [Gavin] God,

00:03:15.868 --> 00:03:17.006
it's got to be putting tremendous strain

00:03:17.006 --> 00:03:19.384
on the springs at this point.

00:03:19.384 --> 00:03:21.906
Should we have safety
goggles, do you think?

00:03:21.906 --> 00:03:22.739
- What for?

00:03:22.739 --> 00:03:23.572
- [Gavin] Eyes!

00:03:23.572 --> 00:03:25.626
- Right, if you left me here,

00:03:25.626 --> 00:03:27.559
and just turned the hose off, right?

00:03:27.559 --> 00:03:28.792
I'd starve to death.

00:03:30.181 --> 00:03:31.522
- That'd be it

00:03:31.522 --> 00:03:33.088
- [Gavin] Oh dear.

00:03:33.088 --> 00:03:34.797
- Oh bugger.

00:03:34.797 --> 00:03:35.855
- [Gavin] What?

00:03:35.855 --> 00:03:37.799
- I'm getting pins and needles in my feet.

00:03:37.799 --> 00:03:39.406
- It's like cutting off the
blood circulation to my legs.

00:03:39.406 --> 00:03:40.239
- [Gavin] We're going to have to amputate.

00:03:40.239 --> 00:03:41.258
- Aw.

00:03:41.258 --> 00:03:43.386
This is definitely one of
those moments in my life

00:03:43.386 --> 00:03:45.410
where I'm like, how did I
find myself in this situation?

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:46.639
I might take those goggles, you know?

00:03:46.639 --> 00:03:47.938
- [Gavin] Yeah?

00:03:47.938 --> 00:03:49.171
- Yeah.

00:03:49.171 --> 00:03:51.190
I think I much preferred being in it.

00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:54.059
Because it's over my knees, yeah?

00:03:54.059 --> 00:03:55.055
- [Gavin] Yeah?

00:03:55.055 --> 00:03:56.651
- It's like bending my knees
backwards the wrong way.

00:03:58.159 --> 00:03:59.497
- Because...

00:03:59.497 --> 00:04:02.058
Because the trampoline does that,

00:04:02.058 --> 00:04:03.012
my legs are like that,

00:04:03.012 --> 00:04:04.088
and the balloons pressing on them.

00:04:04.088 --> 00:04:06.598
Which means that my legs are
like being bent backwards.

00:04:06.598 --> 00:04:07.431
- [Gavin] Hup.

00:04:07.431 --> 00:04:08.264
- Oh.

00:04:10.522 --> 00:04:11.441
- [Gavin] SPF 30.

00:04:11.441 --> 00:04:12.274
- Oh nice.

00:04:16.414 --> 00:04:18.164
I can't get them now!

00:04:25.307 --> 00:04:26.552
- [Gavin] I think we've
got to call this one...

00:04:26.552 --> 00:04:27.385
- Oh!

00:04:29.012 --> 00:04:31.706
- [Gavin] ...crushed by
a 6 foot water balloon.

00:04:31.706 --> 00:04:34.037
- Oh flip.

00:04:34.037 --> 00:04:35.775
- [Gavin] You look like a Mr. Man.

00:04:36.817 --> 00:04:39.568
- [Gavin] Which one of the
Mr. Men was a red circle?

00:04:39.568 --> 00:04:42.080
- Oh! Mr. Amputate My Leg.

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:42.951
Ah!

00:04:42.951 --> 00:04:44.084
- [Gavin] It's so big now.

00:04:44.084 --> 00:04:45.872
- The thing is, I can't even re-adjust it.

00:04:47.752 --> 00:04:50.516
- Ow!

00:04:50.516 --> 00:04:51.513
Oh my leg!

00:04:51.513 --> 00:04:53.332
It's like, twisted.

00:04:53.332 --> 00:04:55.772
Can you itch my foot?

00:04:55.772 --> 00:04:57.022
- [Gavin] Yeah.

00:04:58.004 --> 00:04:58.974
- Ah, oh!

00:04:58.974 --> 00:05:00.286
To the left.

00:05:00.286 --> 00:05:02.286
- [Gavin] Oh come on now.

00:05:02.286 --> 00:05:04.371
- Oh yeah, that's it. There you go.

00:05:04.371 --> 00:05:05.204
Sod that.

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:06.037
- [Gavin] All right,
are you ditching them?

00:05:06.037 --> 00:05:06.870
- They're just annoying me.

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:07.703
- [Gavin] Yeah.

00:05:07.703 --> 00:05:09.577
- If I get my eyes taken out by a balloon,

00:05:09.577 --> 00:05:11.554
I want some sort of compensation.

00:05:11.554 --> 00:05:12.912
- [Gavin] From me?

00:05:12.912 --> 00:05:13.745
- Yeah.

00:05:13.745 --> 00:05:15.378
Have you got the good ones on?

00:05:15.378 --> 00:05:16.331
Give me the good ones.
- Oh Yes.

00:05:16.331 --> 00:05:17.401
You don't even need them,

00:05:17.401 --> 00:05:18.555
what are you wearing them for?

00:05:18.555 --> 00:05:19.740
- [Gavin] No, I'm not
wearing them for the balloon,

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:20.962
I'm wearing them for
the springs flying out.

00:05:20.962 --> 00:05:22.638
- The springs? They'll be fine.

00:05:22.638 --> 00:05:24.007
I might have to pop it soon.

00:05:24.007 --> 00:05:25.190
- [Gavin] Yeah?

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:26.779
Just for your own safety?

00:05:26.779 --> 00:05:27.852
- Yeah, just for my leg.

00:05:27.852 --> 00:05:29.270
I don't want an amputated left leg.

00:05:41.803 --> 00:05:42.636
I'm done.

00:05:42.636 --> 00:05:43.469
- [Gavin] You done?

00:05:43.469 --> 00:05:44.820
- My leg needs to, it's going
to come off in a minute.

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:47.693
- [Gavin] All right, I'll get you out.

00:05:47.693 --> 00:05:49.425
- Show me how you want me to do it.

00:05:49.425 --> 00:05:50.258
Like here?

00:05:50.258 --> 00:05:51.091
- [Gavin] Yep.

00:05:51.091 --> 00:05:51.924
- Yeah?

00:05:51.924 --> 00:05:53.051
- [Gavin] Yep.

00:06:47.434 --> 00:06:48.267
Right, here?

00:06:48.267 --> 00:06:49.100
- [Gavin] Yep.

00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:49.933
- Yeah?
- Yep.

00:06:58.717 --> 00:06:59.800
How was that?

00:07:01.102 --> 00:07:04.057
- I felt like I was
drowning for a second there.

00:07:04.057 --> 00:07:06.644
Because it pops, and
the water went over me,

00:07:06.644 --> 00:07:07.618
it went like

00:07:10.418 --> 00:07:11.913
- [Gavin] Thoughts?

00:07:11.913 --> 00:07:14.621
- Hang on, let me just stand up.

00:07:14.621 --> 00:07:16.481
Oh my god, that left leg.

00:07:22.715 --> 00:07:25.052
- [Gavin] It gave you jelly legs.

00:07:25.052 --> 00:07:26.199
- It did.

00:07:26.199 --> 00:07:27.945
Hang on.

00:07:27.945 --> 00:07:30.169
I'm just letting the blood
re-flush back into my legs.

00:07:30.169 --> 00:07:32.867
- [Gavin] You almost lost
a leg from a balloon!

00:07:32.867 --> 00:07:35.049
- Oh god, I can't move!

00:07:35.049 --> 00:07:37.775
- [Gavin] Dan, the things you
go through for this channel

00:07:38.668 --> 00:07:39.583
- [Gavin] Commendable.

00:07:39.583 --> 00:07:42.220
You know when people
take their first steps

00:07:42.220 --> 00:07:44.006
after spending like a year in space?

00:07:44.006 --> 00:07:44.839
- Like Bambi.

00:07:44.839 --> 00:07:45.672
- [Gavin] Yeah.

00:07:45.672 --> 00:07:47.499
- Okay, yeah. I think I'm good.

00:07:47.499 --> 00:07:48.510
- You can stand again.

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:49.823
- Oh just about.

00:07:49.823 --> 00:07:52.311
- I've never seen jelly legs like that.

00:07:52.311 --> 00:07:53.863
You know how you see like
marathon runners get that?

00:07:53.863 --> 00:07:54.987
- Yeah, I had Bambi legs.

00:07:54.987 --> 00:07:56.703
I had nothing there,

00:07:56.703 --> 00:07:58.088
for about five minutes.
- God, I wonder how

00:07:58.088 --> 00:07:59.720
far away we were from
some permanent damage.

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:00.553
- Oh, it's like your ball

00:08:00.553 --> 00:08:02.214
when that got twisted
around its own blood supply

00:08:02.214 --> 00:08:03.191
and got cut off.

00:08:04.281 --> 00:08:06.281
- Except it was the
entirety of my lower leg

00:08:06.281 --> 00:08:07.411
that I couldn't feel anymore.

00:08:07.411 --> 00:08:09.665
- God, brutal, and it's
just water as well!

00:08:09.665 --> 00:08:11.076
- Well, it's because the trampoline,

00:08:11.076 --> 00:08:12.039
it actually made it worse,

00:08:12.039 --> 00:08:16.452
because my leg was bent
under the weight like that.

00:08:16.452 --> 00:08:17.874
So it was like going the wrong way.

00:08:17.874 --> 00:08:20.526
- You can just never
underestimate the weight of water.

00:08:20.526 --> 00:08:23.211
Like, if that was dropped
from above onto your head,

00:08:23.211 --> 00:08:24.327
it would be like getting hit with a brick.

00:08:24.327 --> 00:08:25.160
- It would kill me.

00:08:25.160 --> 00:08:26.458
- You would absolutely be killed.

00:08:26.458 --> 00:08:27.791
- Yeah.

00:08:27.791 --> 00:08:29.087
- Well, that was enjoyable.

00:08:29.087 --> 00:08:30.126
- For you, yeah.

00:08:30.126 --> 00:08:31.117
- Yeah. Well, yeah.

00:08:31.117 --> 00:08:32.018
- Hopefully for them, too.

00:08:32.018 --> 00:08:33.738
- Hopefully for the audience as well.

00:08:33.738 --> 00:08:34.571
Well done, B.

00:08:34.571 --> 00:08:35.404
- Cheers.

00:08:35.404 --> 00:08:38.771
- And we'll have to crack
on with the other one now.

00:08:38.771 --> 00:08:40.355
- Tune in again for Balloon June...

00:08:40.355 --> 00:08:41.479
- Big Old Balloon June.

00:08:41.479 --> 00:08:42.312
- Next week.

00:08:42.312 --> 00:08:44.804
- Next week, a new
video, a new big balloon.

00:08:44.804 --> 00:08:45.873
- Oh god, I hope I
don't get crushed again.

00:08:45.873 --> 00:08:48.002
- Follow us on Twitter,
subscribe to the main channel,

00:08:48.002 --> 00:08:49.227
second channel.

00:08:49.227 --> 00:08:50.378
- Buy some merch!

00:08:50.378 --> 00:08:51.236
- And buy some merch.

00:08:51.236 --> 00:08:55.164
If Dan sees you wearing that
merch, he will buy you a drink.

00:08:55.164 --> 00:08:55.997
- Probably.

00:08:55.997 --> 00:08:56.981
- See you next week.

